      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T16:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can\u0027t be used with `const`. `cstr!` uses `unwrap()` and it\u0027s prohibited for `const` variables. Here\u0027s relevant compilation error.\n\n```\nerror[E0015]: cannot call non-const fn `Result::\u003c\u0026CStr, FromBytesWithNulError\u003e::unwrap` in constants\n```\n\nI also tried `lazy_static!` but it didn\u0027t support `nostd` in its `Android.bp`.\n\n\nI personally prefer this, but I can change this with const byte literals and calls `cstr!()` whenever it\u0027s necessary. What do you think? Feel free to comment here if you prefer other way.",
      "parentUuid": "97d9077a_df2d981e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "62ae466729963fb073b1f2b484c1d8fe96679117",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0dddf8cc_4788bbf3",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/devices.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T09:04:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why don\u0027t we redefine `cstr` (or introduce a `const_cstr`) as\n\n```\nmacro_rules! cstr {\n    ($str:literal) \u003d\u003e {{\n        #[allow(unused_unsafe)] // In case the macro is used within an unsafe block.\n        unsafe { core::ffi::CStr::from_bytes_with_nul_unchecked(concat!($str, \"\\0\").as_bytes()) }\n    }};\n}\n```\n\nAs the `Safety` comment of `from_bytes_with_nul_unchecked` says that\n\n\u003e The provided slice must be nul-terminated and not contain any interior nul bytes.\n\nthat macro would meet the former while the latter is very unlikely to happen (who\u0027d \"`cstr!(\"xxx\\0yyy\")`\"?!), would be caught by us during review and is actually caught by the compiler in my playground:\n```\n  --\u003e /rustc/d5c2e9c342b358556da91d61ed4133f6f50fc0c3/library/core/src/ffi/c_str.rs:443:17\n   |\n   \u003d note: the evaluated program panicked at \u0027input contained interior nul\u0027, /rustc/d5c2e9c342b358556da91d61ed4133f6f50fc0c3/library/core/src/ffi/c_str.rs:443:17\n   |\nnote: inside `CStr::from_bytes_with_nul_unchecked::const_impl`\n  --\u003e /rustc/d5c2e9c342b358556da91d61ed4133f6f50fc0c3/library/core/src/ffi/c_str.rs:443:17\nnote: inside `CStr::from_bytes_with_nul_unchecked`\n  --\u003e /rustc/d5c2e9c342b358556da91d61ed4133f6f50fc0c3/library/core/src/ffi/c_str.rs:453:18\nnote: inside `A`\n  --\u003e src/main.rs:6:18\n   |\n6  |         unsafe { core::ffi::CStr::from_bytes_with_nul_unchecked(concat!($str, \"\\0\").as_bytes()) }\n   |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n...\n11 |     const A: \u0026CStr \u003d cstr!(\"xxx\\0yyy\");\n   |                      ----------------- in this macro invocation\n   \u003d note: this error originates in the macro `$crate::panic::panic_2021` which comes from the expansion of the macro `cstr`\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a1ee5622_068abb98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "62ae466729963fb073b1f2b484c1d8fe96679117",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
